(3454377, 3597, 73575, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by BigSmiles:</b></div><hr/><i> This is my favourite texture picture for several reasons. There is a dominant S curve in the way the seashells are arranged which makes for awesome composition. There are several noticeable textures within the entire image. The lighting is well done and the DOF was well handled. The arrangement is kept simple and there is nothing complicating the image! Gets a 10 from me. BigSmiles </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Exactly what I would have said if it weren''t easier to quote it! Great texture shot.</td>', 'Originally posted by BigSmiles: This is my favourite texture picture for several reasons. There is a dominant S curve in the way the seashells are arranged which makes for awesome composition. There are several noticeable textures within the entire image. The lighting is well done and the DOF was well handled. The arrangement is kept simple and there is nothing complicating the image! Gets a 10 from me. BigSmiles   Exactly what I would have said if it weren''t easier to quote it! Great texture shot.', '2007-03-12 18:17:27.000000', NULL, 0),
(3462143, 3659, 48228, '<td valign="top">What a grerat find and love images like this..... The detail of the old wood with it peeling paint is amazing, and gives us wonderful textures. The old torn curtain also ads to the aged and run down desolate appearence.....<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2007-03-14 20:22:26.</i></td>', 'What a grerat find and love images like this..... The detail of the old wood with it peeling paint is amazing, and gives us wonderful textures. The old torn curtain also ads to the aged and run down desolate appearence.....', '2007-03-14 20:21:43.000000', '2007-03-14 20:22:26.000000', 0),
(3833523, 3659, 14986, '<td valign="top">Texture indeed!  I like the angle you have chosen here, rather than straight-on.  It seems to give the photo a bit of energy.  I think I would have darkened a bit on some of the peeling paint to add even more to the depth and texture.  Excellent in bw.</td>', 'Texture indeed!  I like the angle you have chosen here, rather than straight-on.  It seems to give the photo a bit of energy.  I think I would have darkened a bit on some of the peeling paint to add even more to the depth and texture.  Excellent in bw.', '2007-06-25 20:43:16.000000', NULL, 0),
