nt to come back for another look?  You know things like that.Technical Aspects:   Focus, exposure, lighting, and other special effects (done by the camera), and post processing are all considered in this category.Meets Challenge:   This is based on my interpretation of if you, have/have not, met the challenge.   This is fairly simple but quite important for this site.There are many sites that can give you assistance in achieving better skills in photography, but I think the best way to learn is to take pictures and show them to other people.   Believe me when it is a good one you will know it.   Good luck!Autool', '2002-07-24 10:03:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(90977, 3468, 1024, '<td valign="top">This photo is more of a snapshot than something I expect to see in a challenge.</td>', 'This photo is more of a snapshot than something I expect to see in a challenge.', '2002-07-24 10:54:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(90978, 3468, 2172, '<td valign="top">Not bad.  For me, it looks too much like a ''snapshot''.  Something I may do, at least for ''texture'' challenge, is to crop and focus on one thing, say the deer to the left, and maybe emphasize the antlers.  Sometimes, for me, taking a snapshot and cropping it can really change the image dramatically.<br/>Still great work!<br/>Ruthann</td>', 'Not bad.  For me, it looks too much like a ''snapshot''.  Something I may do, at least for ''texture'' challenge, is to crop and focus on one thing, say the deer to the left, and maybe emphasize the antlers.  Sometimes, for me, taking a snapshot and cropping it can really change the image dramatically.Still great work!Ruthann', '2002-07-24 13:39:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(90979, 3468, 2586, '<td valign="top">This meets the Texture challenge requirement but only because you say so in the title. I KNOW antlers have that velvety texture but I can''t detect it from looking at this picture. You would have a much better pic for this challenge if you had cropped to only have the head of the left guy and showing  good close up focus of those velvety antlers. This pic has a snapshot quality to it.</td>', 'This meets the Texture challenge requirement but only because you say so in the title. I KNOW antlers have that velvety texture but I can''t detect it from looking at this picture. You would have a much better pic for this challenge if you had cropped to only have the head of the left guy and showing  good close up focus of those velvety antlers. This pic has a snapshot quality to it.', '2002-07-24 13:41:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(90980, 3468, 2634, '<td valign="top">Doesn''t fit the challenge. If it was a better picture of a dear(close up, brighter, more interesting) it would score higher.</td>', 'Doesn''t fit the challenge. If it was a better picture of a dear(close up, brighter, more interesting) it would score higher.', '2002-07-24 13:45:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(90981, 3468, 573, '<td valign="top">The human eye can see the velvet from this distance and lighting angle because the brain puts that texture information in when it processes the image.  The camera has to be right in its face to see texture.</td>', 'The human eye can see the velvet from this distance and lighting angle because the brain puts that texture information in when it processes the image.  The camera has to be right in its face to see texture.', '2002-07-24 14:34:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(90982, 3468, 2302, '<td valign="top">nice photo, but it seems more incidental that you have captured the velvet antlers here. I just don''t see the texture as the main focus - but give you points for getting a good shot = 4</td>', 'nice photo, but it seems more incidental that you have captured the velvet antlers here. I just don''t see the texture as the main focus - but give you points for getting a good shot = 4', '2002-07-24 15:34:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(90983, 3468, 2716, '<td valign="top">Nice picture, however a close up would have dealt better with the topic.</td>', 'Nice picture, however a close up would have dealt better with the topic.', '2002-07-24 15:42:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(90984, 3468, 741, '<td valign="top">Well yes, they have velvet antlers but tat really isn''t obvious from this picture.<br/>Focussing on the deer is pretty soft and composition could be better - they are both looking out of the frame in different directions which makes for a confusing picture and the right deer is very close to the edge of the shot.</td>', 'Well yes, they have velvet antlers but tat really isn''t obvious from this picture.Focussing on the deer is pretty soft and composition could be better - they are both looking out of the frame in different directions which makes for a confusing picture and the right deer is very close to the edge of the shot.', '2002-07-24 15:58:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(90985, 3468, 2764, '<td valign="top">Perhaps the experience of photographing the deer was more exciting than the finished product.  Too many distractions, like the white post and the wite lines and the guard rail that cuts off their feet.  Also it seems crowded on the left.  Could it have been cropped wider?  Unfortunelately a photo is only as good as it''s WORST element.</td>', 'Perhaps the experience of photographing the deer was more exciting than the finished product.  Too many distractions, like the white post and the wite lines and the guard rail that cuts off their feet.  Also it seems crowded on the left.  Could it have been cropped wider?  Unfortunelately a photo is only as good as it''s WORST element.', '2002-07-24 17:22:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(90986, 3468, 2204, '<td valign="top">I get the "idea" that texture is here but, I don''t get the "feel" of texture in this picture.</td>', 'I get the "idea" that texture is here but, I don''t get the "feel" of texture in this picture.', '2002-07-24 18:01:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(90987, 3468, 2311, '<td valign="top">love it...</td>', 'love it...', '2002-07-24 21:56:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(90988, 3468, 1031, '<td valign="top">I might have chosen a closer shot of one of the deer if possible.</td>', 'I might have chosen a closer shot of one of the deer if possible.', '2002-07-25 04:21:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(90989, 3468, 2344, '<td valign="top">Do you have a powerful zoom lens on your camera or did you just get pretty close to those animals? It''s a shame that other people on the site can''t appreciate wildlife like people from northern Canada and other forested areas.</td>', 'Do you have a powerful zoom lens on your camera or did you just get pretty close to those animals? It''s a shame that other people on the site can''t appreciate wildlife like people from northern Canada and other forested areas.', '2002-07-25 09:00:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(90990, 3468, 772, '<td valign="top">I saw your post in the forums about this photo and would like to comment... first of all, whether or not this is a ''difficult'' or ''unique'' photograph is basically irrelevant to the ''challenge'' concept.  I can see why you may have received comments on this issue.  Even though it is very unusual that you were able to get this photo, it doesn''t apply in the challenge.  Even though these deer do have ''velvet'' antlers, you can''t see the texture of it in this photograph.  Try to imagine this photograph with a title of "untitled" being entered in this texture challenge.... It''s a case of the title saving the photo.  The subject of the photo is not a ''texture'' subject, even though it has texture... it''s not readily visible to the viewer.  You could have named this photo "the rough asphalt" or "tree leaves textures" or "fur texture" or anything else along those lines and gotten the same result.  I''m sorry to hear that your luck with this image is not good this week :) = 5 - jmsetzler</td>', 'I saw your post in the forums about this photo and would like to comment... first of all, whether or not this is a ''difficult'' or ''unique'' photograph is basically irrelevant to the ''challenge'' concept.  I can see why you may have received comments on this issue.  Even though it is very unusual that you were able to get this photo, it doesn''t apply in the challenge.  Even though these deer do have ''velvet'' antlers, you can''t see the texture of it in this photograph.  Try to imagine this photograph with a title of "untitled" being entered in this texture challenge.... It''s a case of the title saving the photo.  The subject of the photo is not a ''texture'' subject, even though it has texture... it''s not readily visible to the viewer.  You could have named this photo "the rough asphalt" or "tree leaves textures" or "fur texture" or anything else along those lines and gotten the same result.  I''m sorry to hear that your luck with this image is not good this week :) = 5 - jmsetzler', '2002-07-25 20:40:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(90991, 3468, 2791, '<td valign="top">is that a texture??</td>', 'is that a texture??', '2002-07-26 02:46:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(90992, 3468, 121, '<td valign="top">It''s a decent photo but if you hadn''t given it a title would we have known where to look? I realise the problems of getting close to this subject your lucky to be able to find subjects like this.</td>', 'It''s a decent photo but if you hadn''t given it a title would we have known where to look? I realise the problems of getting close to this subject your lucky to be able to find subjects like this.', '2002-07-26 15:59:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(90993, 3468, 2481, '<td valign="top">texture of antlers lost in space of photo; if you could have gotten right up close to those antlers, it might have worked - but they weren''t about to stay still for that were they? Interesting shot though -</td>', 'texture of antlers lost in space of photo; if you could have gotten right up close to those antlers, it might have worked - but they weren''t about to stay still for that were they? Interesting shot though -', '2002-07-27 23:13:00.000000', NULL, 1),
