(92862, 3611, 2891, '<td valign="top">An actual texture.  Nice close-up/macro.</td>', 'An actual texture.  Nice close-up/macro.', '2002-07-23 16:31:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(92863, 3611, 885, '<td valign="top">Good job of bringing out the texture in the cement.  I like how you put it on the diagonal.  For me, though, this picture needs a bit more interest.  I think the cement would make very interesting negative space for something colored or with some sort of opposite texture.</td>', 'Good job of bringing out the texture in the cement.  I like how you put it on the diagonal.  For me, though, this picture needs a bit more interest.  I think the cement would make very interesting negative space for something colored or with some sort of opposite texture.', '2002-07-23 19:48:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(92864, 3611, 2881, '<td valign="top">Yes, this is my idea of a study in texture! You can feel it without even touching it!</td>', 'Yes, this is my idea of a study in texture! You can feel it without even touching it!', '2002-07-23 19:58:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(92865, 3611, 811, '<td valign="top">It does have texture, and you have done well by having the "grain" move diagonally instead of vertically or horizontally, I think.  It just seems a little monotonous.  Maybe if you had added something that would contrast with both texture and color it would have more "grab appeal."  karmat</td>', 'It does have texture, and you have done well by having the "grain" move diagonally instead of vertically or horizontally, I think.  It just seems a little monotonous.  Maybe if you had added something that would contrast with both texture and color it would have more "grab appeal."  karmat', '2002-07-23 22:58:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(92866, 3611, 1944, '<td valign="top">Your shot has possibilities, but you didn''t exploit them. I would have set the lighter cement colors as white and kept the shadows black. Then it would have had more power. Also, a picture like this should be brutally sharp.</td>', 'Your shot has possibilities, but you didn''t exploit them. I would have set the lighter cement colors as white and kept the shadows black. Then it would have had more power. Also, a picture like this should be brutally sharp.', '2002-07-24 01:20:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(92867, 3611, 1, '<td valign="top">Hehe, nice title.  Nice framing job, the diagnol lines work well in your 3:2 ratio''d image.</td>', 'Hehe, nice title.  Nice framing job, the diagnol lines work well in your 3:2 ratio''d image.', '2002-07-24 11:15:00.000000', NULL, 1),
